```java
-  public void reload() {
-    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
-      ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
```
Reason:
The removal of the `reloadText()` method call in the `reload()` function meant that the help text for commands was no longer being updated. This led to inconsistencies or missing help text when the `/help` command was invoked, as the necessary updates to the help text were not being executed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
public void reload() {
    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
    }
    for (PlayerCommand playerCommand : playerCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) playerCommand).reloadText();
    }
}
```
Reason:
Reintroducing the `reloadText()` method calls ensures that the help text for both server and player commands is properly updated whenever the `reload()` method is invoked. This restores the functionality that was lost with the removal of the method, ensuring that the `/help` command provides accurate and up-to-date information.

